  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are strict on reporting (S1) and recall (S5), with a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger and prompt customer notices. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% action threshold but no automatic sales ban, and gives exact per-model results to owners/regulators while barring public publication; S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit 'where technically feasible'. All four red lines are satisfied, but S2 and S3 contain weakened elements favoring Northwind, while S5's mandatory recall and S4's suppression cost fall more heavily on Halcyon."
 },
